    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Zurich Zebras highlights a clear strategy of prioritizing aggressive baserunning and high-upside platoon splits. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leads our lineup with an elite 82.13 projection; his combination of a favorable matchup against Pallante and the significant boost from a slow pitcher delivery makes him our primary weapon for stealing the SB category. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (73.90) and **Junior Caminero** (73.42) are high-ceiling anchors today. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.425 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** faces Ure\u00f1a, whose 4.58 xERA provides the perfect environment for a breakout offensive performance. We are also leaning heavily on **Kazuma Okamoto** (67.98), who gains a massive 16% park factor bump, making him a cornerstone of our infield production.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge**, who posted a respectable 50.59. Despite the wind-aided boost and leadoff spot, he ultimately fell short of the threshold compared to the platoon-advantaged **Casey Schmitt** and **Christian Yelich**. We are closely monitoring the lineup pending status for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**; while their respective 62.08 and 60.36 scores are solid, both are facing Wrobleski, and we are banking on the projected wind-out conditions at the park to maintain their viability. We must remain cautious with **Caleb Durbin**; while his 52.44 score is bolstered by his speed, he faces an elite catcher with a 1.86s pop time, which creates a tactical risk for his SB potential. As always, **Lars Nootbaar** remains sidelined, and we continue to rotate our depth to protect against game cap depletion.",
